Id: shl001w
Severity: WARN
Category: filesystem
Check: check_shells
Fix: Set TMOUT in /etc/profile and autologout in /etc/csh.login.
References: bash(1), tcsh(1)
Controls: CIS 4.3; NIST AC-12; ISO 8.5; CE User access control

No shell idle timeout is set: neither TMOUT in the Bourne-family
startup nor autologout in the C-shell startup, so an idle session
never dies, and whoever walks up to it is the user. Set TMOUT in
/etc/profile (TMOUT=600; readonly TMOUT; export TMOUT) and
autologout in /etc/csh.login for the C shells.
